{"id": "EUVD-2026-103604", "enisaUuid": "cb2a30dc-8b65-3713-8ab6-f514c22fc026", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: fix UAF on lgr list traversal in smcr_port_err()\n\nsmcr_port_err() traverses smc_lgr_list.list without holding\nsmc_lgr_list.lock, allowing a concurrent smc_lgr_terminate_sched()\nto free an lgr while it is still being dereferenced.\n\nHold smc_lgr_list.lock across the traversal. Update\nsmc_ib_gid_check() to call smcr_port_err() after releasing the lock.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:43", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/34bcf11cd2528ae00bb6d764d808083c66824277", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0edcc4284392b28826b5d37532b366b291e6e0fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00a59600ae72d24859d0ad1783a78bc921bc2599", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d35f069e1c119992000d51236dbe54da2d4e61e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d65a2eb4449fc9658fb860dea893025d028d90e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9b968e42690d784c241a0761c10253271f7df5d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61cb282fe97b3b0ba32ca09417a693162bf4ae3f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4x5q-83g5-68jv", "CVE-2026-98559"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00e7ffcb-320a-3a93-94c1-436d2d8b5b28", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "541afa10c126b6c22c2a805a559c70cc41fd156e <a9b968e42690d784c241a0761c10253271f7df5d"}, {"id": "01b182e1-a401-3bb1-a9ba-788bb00751f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "056ec40c-b007-3992-bc6c-fa3bfe08f949", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "28ba55e9-a185-3149-82b2-771f0c8f5ddd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "2bbc3b76-807c-342a-8462-e39b68c16a6b", "product": {"name": "Li